    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avenue Zero is a 1v1 competitive arena fighter designed with a simple goal: give fighting game players a system worth mastering. This isn\u2019t a button-masher or a cinematic shortcut engine. It\u2019s a movement-conscious, state-driven combat system inspired by the best aspects of: Tenkaichi\u2019s directional commitment and movement freedom.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Development Status</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avenue Zero is currently in early pre-alpha. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We're in the process of building out and refining the core combat systems\u2014Measure and Anchor states, Impulse timing, directional pressure, and Flow mechanics\u2014before expanding into full campaign content or large-scale art production. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Our focus is mechanical first: </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every system is being designed to support competitive integrity, expressive play, and clean feedback. The goal is to build a foundation that can hold up under serious labbing and high-level match pacing. We\u2019re not starting from spectacle\u2014we\u2019re starting from substance. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Our Long-Term Vision</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avenue Zero is built from a high-ambition blueprint: </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A competitive-first 1v1 fighter </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A full-featured campaign mode with ensemble characters </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A city-scale world driven by an original genre: Jack City Punk </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A system that grows with the community and supports serious skill development</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avenue Zero is a 1v1 competitive arena fighter designed with a simple goal: give fighting game players a system worth mastering. This isn\u2019t a button-masher or a cinematic shortcut engine. It\u2019s a movement-conscious, state-driven combat system inspired by the best aspects of: Tenkaichi\u2019s directional commitment and movement freedom.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Development Status</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avenue Zero is currently in early pre-alpha. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We're in the process of building out and refining the core combat systems\u2014Measure and Anchor states, Impulse timing, directional pressure, and Flow mechanics\u2014before expanding into full campaign content or large-scale art production. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Our focus is mechanical first: </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every system is being designed to support competitive integrity, expressive play, and clean feedback. The goal is to build a foundation that can hold up under serious labbing and high-level match pacing. We\u2019re not starting from spectacle\u2014we\u2019re starting from substance. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Our Long-Term Vision</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avenue Zero is built from a high-ambition blueprint: </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A competitive-first 1v1 fighter </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A full-featured campaign mode with ensemble characters </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A city-scale world driven by an original genre: Jack City Punk </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A system that grows with the community and supports serious skill development</p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Avenue Zero is a 1v1 competitive arena fighter built for players who want real depth, clean mechanics, and a complete analog-futurist world to explore. High-skill combat, expressive systems, and a story-rich environment built in a new genre: Jack City Punk.",
